[style name="Interaction_Style"]
if {Ian.Confrontationn_at_home} == 1:
	join Thorinn (normal) leftmost
	*Knock knock*
	Ian: Come in.
	[background arg="res://gui/Dialog/styles/Finished_Ian_room.webp" fade="0.0"]
	join Ian rightmost
	Thorinn: Good morning. My name is Thorinn, I am a traveling doctor. Hugo sent me, he said you’ve fallen ill.
	Ian: Thorinn... I’ve heard that name before. Where did you study medicine?
	Thorinn: I trained in Baltimore under Master Galbraith.
	Ian (angry): Of course. Galbraith never stopped talking about his ‘most promising student.’
	Thorinn (surprised): So he talked about me? I guess you are lucky to have me then... haha.
	*A moment of awkward silence*
	Thorinn (normal): That's the reason I'm here. Our master has taught me well, and I’ve saved many lives. Including yours, if you’ll let me.
	Ian (angry): And why would you want to save me? What is your motive? You could take my place as the trusted healer the moment I’m gone or even help death along a little faster.
	Thorinn (normal): You overestimate my cruelty. I don’t need to hasten your death, Ian. The villagers will come to me in time, because they’ll see I’m more capable.
	Thorinn: But I came here because it’s what a doctor does. I heal. I leave the rest to fate.
	Ian (normal): Fate? You talk as though you don’t have a hand in it. You’ve been searching for an opportunity like this, haven’t you? To step in and become the savior of a village.
	- Try to save Ian
		Thorinn (agitated): I don’t need to take what’s already slipping from your grasp, Ian. This village doesn’t need someone clinging to old ways. They need someone who can do more...
		Thorinn: ...someone who can truly save them. They need me. And I will do whatever is necessary to protect them.
		Ian (sceming): Save them? I’ve cared for these people for years, Thorinn. I know their needs better than you ever will.
		Thorinn (agitated): You’ve cared for them, yes. But have you healed them? Look around, Ian. The village is wasting away, just like you.
		Thorinn: You hold onto traditions that no longer work. Soon, they will see it too. They’ll come to me, because they’ll have no other choice.
		Ian (angry): So why save me, then? If you’re so sure they’ll turn to you, why bother? To ease your conscience? Or so I can live long enough to watch you take everything from me?
		Thorinn (normal): I am treating you because that's my job, I heal people.
		Ian (angry): You arrogant fool. Do you think this will make them trust you? I’ll tell them what kind of man you are. I’ll make sure they see the truth.
		Thorinn (agitated): We’ll see. Now lie still. You don’t have much time, and I won’t let my first victory here be a failure.
		leave --All--
		Thorinn retrieves his medical supplies from the Inn, but by the time he gets back to the pharmacy Ian has already passed.
	- End Ian’s Suffering
		*Thorinn calmly, pulling a small vial from his bag.*
		Thorinn (normal): But by then, it’ll be too late for you to see it. I’ve prepared something...a final act of mercy from one healer to another. It will ease your pain.
		Ian (angry): What... what is that?
		Thorinn (normal): A blend of rare herbs, taught to me by our master. It will calm your body; let you rest and make your life come to a peaceful end.
		Ian (angry): That’s pathetic, you think I will just give up now?
		Thorinn (normal): Drink, Ian. Let it be peaceful.
		Ian (normal): You know Thorinn, you might be right. I think it ends here, but please don’t tell the villagers of my cowardice.
		Thorinn (surprised): If that’s the cost, so be it. For now, let me end your suffering. 
		Ian, too weak to resist, takes the vial and drinks. His face twists as the liquid burns through him, his breaths becoming shallow and labored.
		Ian (angry): Treat my people well Thorinn, the village is in your hands now....
		Thorinn (agitated): Don’t worry, they’re in good hands. Rest, Ian. You’ll find peace soon.
		Ian’s body goes limp, his breath slowing until it stops. Thorinn watches for a moment, his face unreadable, before standing and turning away. He leaves the pharmacy without a word, stepping into the quiet streets of the village.
	- Refuse to Help
		Thorinn (agitated): Ian, I didn’t come to take anything from you. I just came to help; I came here out of respect.
		Ian (angry): Respect? Is that what you call this? Do you really wish to say that our master has taught you more and better than me?
		Thorinn (normal): I was his best student after all, Ian. But that doesn’t make me your enemy. Now tell me, do you wish for me to help you or not?
		Ian (angry): Does it really seem like I need your help? I can take care of myself!
		Thorinn (agitated): Then I won’t, if that’s what you wish, but know that I’ll take over your pharmacy sooner or later.
		Thorinn (normal): You’ve given the village your life, Ian, and no one will forget that. But their needs have grown beyond what you can offer. 
		Thorinn (normal): And they will turn to me, whether you survive or not.
		Ian (sceming): That remains to be seen, now leave me be. I don’t feel like hearing anymore of your arrogant remarks.
		Ian stares at Thorinn, his breathing slowing as his strength fades. Thorinn stands for a moment, watching, his expression heavy with unspoken emotion. He finally turns to leave. 
		leave Ian
		Thorinn (agitated): Very well, Ian. I’ll leave. The village will remember you...
		Thorinn leaves Ian to his fate. Ian dies shortly after.
